tree-sitter-snowflake adapts material from two MIT-licensed projects.

The external scanner for dollar-quoted strings (src/scanner.c) derives from
DerekStride/tree-sitter-sql's scanner (https://github.com/DerekStride/tree-sitter-sql),
copyright (c) 2021 Derek Stride, licensed under the MIT License. The
adaptation is substantial: Snowflake supports only the bare `$$` delimiter —
not PostgreSQL's `$tag$` form — so the tag-carrying state machine was
removed and the token set reduced to the three the Snowflake body shape
needs.

The repository scaffold (module layout under grammar/, the option-list and
keyword-extraction conventions, the Rust and Node bindings, and the CI
shape) follows tree-sitter-mssql
(https://github.com/meloncholic/tree-sitter-mssql), itself a fork of
DerekStride/tree-sitter-sql; its grammar modules were used as style
reference for rule organization, and node naming for constructs common to
both dialects echoes the general-SQL naming so existing consumer profiles
transfer with minimal change.

